 "text": "Hey, how are you holding up? Keep it in the refrigerator, it' much colder than a cupboard. Blocks are the best, they keep the longest. Fill a plastic bag with ice cubes and throw in some salt, they'll melt much faster. Keep it well wrapped and get it out just long enough for each drink. And don't over stuff it, eventually the cold air you let out has to be replaced. Let him keep it in the fridge, and get a nice cool bag of iced water for himself. Pour it down the sink and fill the container up again with fresh cold water. It's wasteful otherwise.",
